    crm:P67i_is_referred_to_by [ a crm:E33_Linguistic_Object ;
            crm:P190_has_symbolic_content "kip, a bundle or set of hides, skins or furs, used as a measure of quantity (OED s.v. kip n.1); e.g. a kip of lambfells reckoned at 150 lambskins. Frequently confused orthographically with kipe (a basket) — see kyppe." ;
